", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 6.35, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u05s1a02", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. Use the digits 1, 4, 6, 8 once each to make two numbers like _._ with the largest possible total. What is the total?", "diff": "VH", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 14.5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "Put 8 and 6 in the ones places.", "reason": "e.g. 8.4 + 6.1 = 14.5."}, {"id": "m5u05s1a03", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. A number minus 2.75 is 4.5. The number?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 7.25, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}], "more": [{"id": "m5u05s1m01", "type": "num", "prompt": "1.1 + 2.2?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3.3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u05s1m02", "type": "num", "prompt": "5.5 − 2.5?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u05s1m03", "type": "num", "prompt": "0.7 + 0.6?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 1.3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u05s1m04", "type": "num", "prompt": "4 − 1.5?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2.5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u05s1m05", "type": "num", "prompt": "2.25 + 0.75?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u05s1m06", "type": "num", "prompt": "1000 − 250?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 750, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}], "notes": "v4", "pdf": [{"book": "c5u05", "p0": 2, "p1": 5, "label": "pages 2–5", "title": "Lesson 5.1 notes · Addition and subtraction including decimal numbers", "note": "The whole lesson as a document you can print, then Practice on paper with answers at the back.", "look": []}]}, {"id": "5.2", "title": "Addition and subtraction of positive and negative numbers", "objs": ["O2"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Freezer", "p": ["The freezer shows **−18 °C**. When the door is left open, the temperature rises by **7 degrees**.", "What does the display show now? Think about it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Negative numbers", "p": ["On a number line, −5 is 5 steps left of 0."], "qq": {"id": "m5u05s2t01", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Colder?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "−5 °C", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "−2 °C", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Moving on a number line", "p": ["**Adding** moves **right** (up); **subtracting** moves **left** (down).", "−18 + 7: start at −18, move 7 right → **−11 °C**."], "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": -5, "max": 5, "mark": -2}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Crossing zero", "p": ["−3 + 5: 3 steps to 0, then 2 more → **2**. 4 − 6: 4 steps to 0, then 2 more → **−2**."], "table": {"head": ["Calculation", "Answer"], "rows": [["−6 + 4", "−2"], ["−2 + 9", "7"], ["3 − 8", "−5"], ["−1 − 4", "−5"]]}}, {"k": "try", "t": "Number line", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m5u05s2t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out −4 + 6.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "2."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I add and subtract with negative numbers?", "p": ["Step 1: Picture a number line.", "Step 2: Start at the first number.", "Step 3: Add → move right; subtract → move left.", "Step 4: Count carefully across zero."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Below zero", "p": [], "q": "−2 − 3.", "steps": [["start at −2, 3 left", ""]], "a": "−5"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Cross zero", "p": [], "q": "5 − 9.", "steps": [["5 to 0, then 4 more left", ""]], "a": "−4"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Temperature rise", "p": [], "q": "From −6 °C to 3 °C. Rise?", "steps": [["6 up to 0, then 3", ""]], "a": "9 degrees"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Lift", "p": [], "q": "Floor 2, down 4 floors.", "steps": [["2 − 4 = −2", ""]], "a": "floor −2 (basement 2)"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Subtract", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m5u05s2t03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 1 − 7.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": -6, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "−6."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Moved the wrong way", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Work out −5 + 3.", "lines": ["start at −5, move left 3 → −8"], "bad": 0, "why": "Adding moves RIGHT: −5 + 3 = −2.", "fix": [["−2", ""]], "id": "m5u05s2t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Going the wrong way along the number line", "p": ["Add → right; subtract → left."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Thermometers, lifts and sea level (−20 m) all use negative numbers."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["Number line: left is smaller.", "Add → right; subtract → left.", "Cross zero in two steps.", "Rise = difference between temperatures."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 660, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "5.2-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u05s2k01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Before you read on: new temperature?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": -11, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "5.2-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u05s2k02", "type": "num", "prompt": "−6 + 4?", "diff"